Subject: Convert audio streams as SDL3 does
Upstream-base: fbe120f5020f8bdcb9cbf5ae28d9859b29781119

The game's sound output (src/platform/ai.cpp) relies on SDL3's streams:
no-copy buffers that complete only once read, a source format that changes
while earlier input still plays at its own rate, gain, an input channel map,
pause and clear, and exact available and queued counts. Streams now keep their
input as it was put, in chunks with their format and map, and convert it when
read: SDL2's format and channel converters around a windowed-sinc resampler of
the layer's own, as SDL2's holds back 512 frames and restarts its phase on
every put. Device streams always pull through the SDL2 callback.

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index a6c30f3..29fb5a1 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -16,15 +16,13 @@ declared in `include/SDL3/s3_defs.h` and `include/SDL3_mixer/s3_mixer_defs.h` ex
 
 ## Known differences from SDL3
 
-- Only the default playback device opens. A device stream opened without a callback queues
-  through SDL2's `SDL_QueueAudio`. SDL2 drains that queue a whole device buffer at a time and
-  fills any shortfall with silence, so an application needs to keep more than one device buffer
-  queued.
-- `SDL_GetAudioStreamQueued` is exact while nothing has been read. SDL2 does not report how much
-  input its resampler has consumed, so after reads the input behind the output is estimated from
-  the rates and frame sizes.
-- An audio stream's format cannot change once it is created; `SDL_SetAudioStreamFormat` is not
-  mapped.
+- Only the default playback device opens. As in SDL3 it is asked for at least S16, stereo and
+  44100 Hz, and its stream converts to whatever format SDL2's driver then reports.
+- Streams convert with SDL2's format and channel converters and the layer's own windowed-sinc
+  resampler, so samples can differ from SDL3's in their last bits. Integer input at an unchanged
+  rate and unity gain comes out unchanged, as in SDL3. A resampled stream holds back its last 8
+  input frames (more when downsampling) until more input or a flush arrives.
+- `SDL_SetAudioStreamGain` and `SDL_GetAudioStreamGain` do not take the stream's lock.
 - Setting a string property to NULL clears its value; it does not delete the property.
 - SDL3 event types with no SDL2 source, such as pen and camera events, are not declared, and
   `SDL_INIT_CAMERA` fails. `SDL_EVENT_FINGER_CANCELED` and the drop events are declared so code
